This is an annual indicator (average of two semesters) and 2022 will be reported when the semester ends.&nbsp;

Although ridership has decreased because of the pandemic, which could affect the average number of passengers per sq meter to meet the maximum train occupancy at the peak of isolation measures, pre-pandemic levels met the target (up to 6) and were below the baseline (8):&nbsp;

2015: 7

2016: 6.5

2017: 6

2018: 6

2019: 6

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The target has been revised in the last restructuring to conform with the maximum demand expected and the maximum train occupancy during the pandemic (about 60% of normal levels).&nbsp;

The frequency of trains pre-pandemic was generally higher between branches but did not meet the previous target.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

This is an annual indicator (average of two semesters)&nbsp;and 2022 will be reported when the semester ends.

Train failures can range from minor breakage up to serious operational disruptions, which affect the overall system&rsquo;s reliability and generates disturbance to users. The inclusion of this indicator aims to measure the improvement in reliability provided by the new trains acquired by the project.

This indicator has been affected by the theft of copper cables because of the economic crisis. Nevertheless, it is 15.8 times&nbsp;the baseline.&nbsp;

